## Story Description
The /cube/by-supplier endpoint returns {data: SupplierRow[], total_count: N}. SupplierPage (line 75) and PaymentTermsPage (line 66) both do .then(r => r.data) and store the whole envelope as SupplierRow[], causing TypeError when .filter()/.sort()/.find()/.reduce() are called on a plain object — this is the root cause of the white page on both pages. Fix both files to extract the nested array and add staleTime:5min to all queries.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/SupplierPage.tsx — in the all-suppliers useQuery (line ~75), change .then(r => r.data) to .then(r => r.data?.data ?? []); add staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000 to all three useQuery calls in this file (all-suppliers, by-month-detail, by-category-detail)
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/PaymentTermsPage.tsx — in the all-suppliers-pt useQuery (line ~66), change .then(r => r.data) to .then(r => r.data?.data ?? []); add staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000 to both useQuery calls. The by-payment-terms query (line ~59) returns a plain array — its .then(r => r.data) is correct, do not change it.
- Verify: the useQuery<SupplierRow[]> type annotation at SupplierPage line 72 still matches after the fix — the return type of .then(r => r.data?.data ?? []) is SupplierRow[] | never[] which is compatible
- Run: cd frontend && npx tsc --noEmit — exits with code 0

